        "original_id": "f43fbd9a-fd14-5f14-a54d-09f2c6ce8ef3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Max Ehrmann\n- Works: Desiderata\n- Places: Terre Haute, Indiana\n- Topics: prose poetry, later popularity\n\nFacts:\n- Max Ehrmann was born on September 26, 1872, and he was an American writer, poet, and attorney from Terre Haute, Indiana.\n- In 1927, Max Ehrmann wrote the prose poem \"Desiderata,\" whose Latin title means \"things desired\" or \"desired things.\"\n- Max Ehrmann was widely known for \"Desiderata,\" although the poem was largely unknown during his lifetime.\n- Max Ehrmann died on September 9, 1945.\n- \"Desiderata\" became widely known after it was used in devotional and spoken-word recordings in 1971 and 1972.",
